From e39286950e2595326ad4f6e093a7f1d1157e5353 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:52:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Back the React app with a PHP + SQLite API built from
 components/

The React app kept its state in localStorage with its own hardcoded seed data,
so it shared nothing with the components/ sketches, hardcorded_data.json or the
SQLite database. Give it a real backend instead.

The PHP is laid out the way a Nextcloud app is (appinfo/, lib/Controller,
lib/Db, templates/) so the move to Nextcloud does not mean rewriting it:

  - lib/Db/Database.php     schema plus an additive import of
                            hardcorded_data.json and rewards.json
  - lib/Db/*Mapper.php      users, chores, assignments, notifications, tiers
  - lib/Service            PointsService (PointHelpers.jsx) and Schedule,
                            which derives due dates and priority from frequency
  - lib/Controller         chores, assignments, users, notifications
  - appinfo/routes.php     the route table, in Nextcloud's format
  - api/index.php          local front controller that dispatches that table

The frontend gains the pieces it never had: per-user point bars with the
add/remove animations, the notification bell, reward tiers, the '+' assign
action, and a details panel. Filters and sorting now run server-side against
the same query the Python port used.

Points work as PointHelpers.jsx documents: base points for the frequency times
days since the chore was last done, capped at 30 days, written to a ledger row
per assignment so reopening a chore takes back exactly what it gave.

Also fills in the empty appinfo/info.xml and Nextcloud stubs, drops the empty
lib/Db/Chore.php and the superseded api/ChoreList.jsx, and scopes oxlint to app
source so the components/ sketches stop failing the lint run.

